{"uid":"3bafa124510c7e75","name":"test_import_agent_valid_md_file","fullName":"tests.ui.agents.test_import_agent_valid_md_file.TestImportAgentValidMdFile#test_import_agent_valid_md_file","historyId":"0a26ffa3136287bcd2a628cd5cb7b726","time":{"start":1789645395976,"stop":1789645408089,"duration":12113},"description":"Import a hand-authored (not app-exported) ``.md`` file and verify\n        the resulting Agent's Name/Description/Instructions/Model all match\n        the source file verbatim.\n\n        The fixture's ``model:`` value is derived at run time from the\n        project's live model catalog (``credential_api.list_models()`` —\n        the same ``GET /configurations/models/{project_id}`` the import\n        wizard itself reads), never hardcoded: an unknown model name is\n        silently replaced by the wizard's ``items[0]`` fallback, so a stale\n        literal turns this assertion into a false red (board #2083). The\n        catalog is used as an ORACLE only — the imported agent's Model is\n        still produced entirely by the product.\n\n        Steps (AFS\n        test-specs/agents/l2_import-valid-agent-md-file-correct-config_ELITEA-1901.md):\n        1. Navigate to the Agents dashboard; verify the ``Agents`` header,\n           the Import button, and that the list region settled into a\n           terminal, non-error state (cards OR the \"No agents yet\" empty\n           state). Makes no claim about pre-existing agents — zero is a\n           valid environment (AFS § Environment Independence).\n        2. Click the Import button and select the hand-authored ``.md``\n           fixture; verify the \"Import parameters\" preview dialog opens.\n        3. Verify the dialog shows an entity card for the agent (name\n           matches the fixture verbatim).\n        4. Confirm the dialog's Import button; verify the \"Import Complete\"\n           success dialog lists the new agent, backed by a\n           ``201 Created`` on the import_wizard endpoint.\n        5. Click \"Got it\"; verify auto-navigation to the new Agent's detail\n           page, then re-open the Agents dashboard and verify a card with\n           the correct name.\n        6. Open the imported agent; verify Name, Description, Instructions,\n           and Model all match the source file verbatim.\n        ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Import a hand-authored (not app-exported) <code>.md</code> file and verify<br />\nthe resulting Agent's Name/Description/Instructions/Model all match<br />\nthe source file verbatim.</p>\n<pre><code>    The fixture's ``model:`` value is derived at run time from the\n    project's live model catalog (``credential_api.list_models()`` —\n    the same ``GET /configurations/models/{project_id}`` the import\n    wizard itself reads), never hardcoded: an unknown model name is\n    silently replaced by the wizard's ``items[0]`` fallback, so a stale\n    literal turns this assertion into a false red (board #2083). The\n    catalog is used as an ORACLE only — the imported agent's Model is\n    still produced entirely by the product.\n\n    Steps (AFS\n    test-specs/agents/l2_import-valid-agent-md-file-correct-config_ELITEA-1901.md):\n    1. Navigate to the Agents dashboard; verify the ``Agents`` header,\n       the Import button, and that the list region settled into a\n       terminal, non-error state (cards OR the &quot;No agents yet&quot; empty\n       state). Makes no claim about pre-existing agents — zero is a\n       valid environment (AFS § Environment Independence).\n    2. Click the Import button and select the hand-authored ``.md``\n       fixture; verify the &quot;Import parameters&quot; preview dialog opens.\n    3. Verify the dialog shows an entity card for the agent (name\n       matches the fixture verbatim).\n    4. Confirm the dialog's Import button; verify the &quot;Import Complete&quot;\n       success dialog lists the new agent, backed by a\n       ``201 Created`` on the import_wizard endpoint.\n    5. Click &quot;Got it&quot;; verify auto-navigation to the new Agent's detail\n       page, then re-open the Agents dashboard and verify a card with\n       the correct name.\n    6. Open the imported agent; verify Name, Description, Instructions,\n       and Model all match the source file verbatim.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":1,"retriesStatusChange":true,"beforeStages":[{"name":"base_url","time":{"start":1789644886821,"stop":1789644886821,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"pytestconfig","time":{"start":1789644886821,"stop":1789644886821,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_verify_url","time":{"start":1789644886821,"stop":1789644886821,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"delete_output_dir","time":{"start":1789644886821,"stop":1789644886821,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"browser","time":{"start":1789644886822,"stop":1789644887272,"duration":450},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"auth_state","time":{"start":1789644887273,"stop":1789644889098,"duration":1825},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{